# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unity — generated folders
#
# Everything here is rebuilt by Unity from Assets/, Packages/ and
# ProjectSettings/. Library/ in particular holds the Cesium tile cache and can
# reach several GB, which is why a Unity repo without this file is unusable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Asset meta data — only ignore meta files for folders that are themselves ignored
!/[Aa]ssets/**/*.meta

# Recordings and crash reports
[Rr]ecordings/
sysinfo.txt
crashlytics-build.properties

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE / build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.idea/
.vsconfig
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
#
# CesiumSettings holds your Cesium ion access token in plain text. Anyone who
# can read it can stream Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles against YOUR ion quota.
#
# Committing it is a deliberate choice, not an accident:
#
#   Ignored (below)  — safest. Each person adds their own free ion token once,
#                      via Cesium > Connect to Cesium ion in Unity. Until they
#                      do, the world is empty.
#   Committed        — convenient. Delete these two lines and your partner sees
#                      the campus immediately, billed to your account. Only do
#                      this in a PRIVATE repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/[Aa]ssets/CesiumSettings/Resources/CesiumIonServers/
/[Aa]ssets/CesiumSettings/Resources/CesiumIonServers.meta

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python analysis outputs
#
# TelemetryData/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the CST499 assignment requires
# the real data to be submitted, and keeping it in the repo makes the analysis
# reproducible. The figures are regenerated by the script, so they are ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
figures/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Unity-generated UI schema
UIElementsSchema/
